Rules in force for supply-chain-codex-chatgpt
File: $T/proj/agent.yaml
Tier: landlock

Can read: Files the agent can open and read.
  Can read any other file on this computer, except the ones under Never reads and Always on.

Can change: Files and folders the agent can create, edit or delete.
  - Can change files in ./src/  [Enforced by the operating system; line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in ./tests/  [Enforced by the operating system; line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in ./vendor/  [Enforced by the operating system; line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in ./tmp/  [Enforced by the operating system; line 33; editable]
  - Can change /dev/null  [Enforced by the operating system; line 33; editable]
  - Can change /dev/tty  [Enforced by the operating system; line 33; editable]
  - Can change /dev/ptmx  [Enforced by the operating system; line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in /dev/pts/  [Enforced by the operating system; line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in ~/codex-home/  [Enforced by the operating system; line 33; editable]
  Cannot change anything else.

Asks you first: The agent waits until you answer on the dashboard.
  - Asks you before it reads ~/.config/telemetry/token  [Enforced: tego holds the action until you answer; line 37; editable]
  - Asks you before it reads files in ./confidential/  [Enforced: tego holds the action until you answer; line 37; editable]
  - Asks you before it changes files in ./held/  [Enforced: tego holds the action until you answer; line 38; editable]
  If you do not answer within 5 minutes, the answer is no.

Never reads: Files the agent can never open, whatever it tries.
  - Can never read ~/.ssh/id_ed25519  [Enforced by the operating system; line 36; editable]

Programs: The programs the agent can start.
  - Can run codex, the command it starts with  [Enforced by the operating system; line 25]
  - Can run bash  [Enforced by the operating system; line 44; editable]
  - Can run git  [Enforced by the operating system; line 45; editable]
  - Can run env  [Enforced by the operating system; line 46; editable]
  - Can run sh  [Enforced by the operating system; line 47; editable]
  - Can run cat  [Enforced by the operating system; line 48; editable]
  - Can run ls  [Enforced by the operating system; line 49; editable]
  - Can run mkdir  [Enforced by the operating system; line 50; editable]
  - Can run touch  [Enforced by the operating system; line 51; editable]
  - Can run grep  [Enforced by the operating system; line 52; editable]
  - Can run sed  [Enforced by the operating system; line 53; editable]
  - Can run head  [Enforced by the operating system; line 54; editable]
  - Can run tail  [Enforced by the operating system; line 55; editable]
  - Can run find  [Enforced by the operating system; line 56; editable]
  - Can run wc  [Enforced by the operating system; line 57; editable]
  - Can run tr  [Enforced by the operating system; line 58; editable]
  - Can run sort  [Enforced by the operating system; line 59; editable]
  - Can run uname  [Enforced by the operating system; line 60; editable]
  - Can run python3  [Enforced by the operating system; line 61; editable]
  - Can run python3.12  [Enforced by the operating system; line 62; editable]
  - Can run codex-code-mode-host  [Enforced by the operating system; line 63; editable]
  Cannot run any other program.

Network: Where the agent can connect.
  - Can connect to 127.0.0.1 on port 8803  [Enforced: tego checks each connection; line 71; editable]
  - Can use the local socket /var/run/nscd/socket  [Enforced: tego checks each connection; line 71; editable]
  - Can connect to chatgpt.com on port 443  [Enforced: tego checks each connection; line 71; editable]
  - Can connect to auth.openai.com on port 443  [Enforced: tego checks each connection; line 71; editable]
  - Cannot send datagrams anywhere it may not connect  [Best effort: tego checks each datagram's address, but sends one it allows by the agent's own call, which a program built to race tego could redirect; built in]
  Cannot connect anywhere else.

Settings it gets: Environment variables the agent starts with, by name. Values are never shown here.
  - Gets PATH from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 76]
  - Gets HOME from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 76]
  - Gets LANG from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 76]
  - Gets TERM from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 76]
  - Gets COLORTERM from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 76]
  - Gets SERVICE_TOKEN from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 76]
  - Gets SC_SINK from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 76]
  - Gets SC_API from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 76]
  - Gets PYTHONPATH from your shell  [Enforced: other variables are removed before the agent starts; line 76]
  - Gets CODEX_HOME, set in its rules  [line 78]
  - Gets HISTFILE, set in its rules  [line 79]
  - Gets TMPDIR, set in its rules  [line 80]
  Every other variable in your shell, secrets included, is removed before it starts.

Limits: When the run is stopped or slowed down.
  - Can run at most 512 processes at once  [line 82]
  - Can use at most 4 GiB of memory  [line 83]
  - Is stopped after 2 hours  [line 84]

Always on: Protections every run gets, written in no rules file.
  - Can never read the usual secret files: SSH and cloud keys, browser profiles, .env files and similar  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Can never read or change tego's records of its runs  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Cannot change its own rules file  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Can read this computer's network setup: interface names and addresses, routes, and the nearby machines it has talked to  [built in]
  - Cannot gain root through sudo or other setuid programs  [Enforced by the operating system; built in]
  - Writes every refusal and question to a record that cannot be changed unnoticed, and a summary of the rest  [built in]

Rule keys:
  change fs.write fs.write[./src/] enforced
  change fs.write fs.write[./tests/] enforced
  change fs.write fs.write[./vendor/] enforced
  change fs.write fs.write[./tmp/] enforced
  change fs.write fs.write[/dev/null] enforced
  change fs.write fs.write[/dev/tty] enforced
  change fs.write fs.write[/dev/ptmx] enforced
  change fs.write fs.write[/dev/pts/] enforced
  change fs.write fs.write[$T/home/codex-home/] enforced
  ask fs.ask_read fs.ask_read[$T/home/.config/telemetry/token] enforced
  ask fs.ask_read fs.ask_read[./confidential/] enforced
  ask fs.ask fs.ask[./held/] enforced
  never-read fs.deny_read fs.deny_read[$T/home/.ssh/id_ed25519] enforced
  programs command exec[codex] enforced (+1 more)
  programs exec.allow exec[bash] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[git] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[env] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[sh] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[cat] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[ls] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[mkdir] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[touch] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[grep] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[sed] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[head] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[tail] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[find] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[wc] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[tr] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[sort] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[uname] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[python3] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[$T/bin/python3.12] enforced
  programs exec.allow exec[$T/bin/codexhost/codex-code-mode-host] enforced
  network net.allow net[127.0.0.1:8803] enforced
  network net.allow net[unix:/var/run/nscd/socket] enforced
  network net.allow net[tcp://chatgpt.com:443] enforced
  network net.allow net[tcp://auth.openai.com:443] enforced
  always-on built-in.deny_read fs.deny_read[$T/home/.ssh] enforced (+1 more)
  always-on built-in.route-read route-query none
